:: Mom Office Blouse [micro_event event nobr] {"position":"1425,3400","size":"100,100"}
/* Inline micro event in the Stage 1 main room (micro event 41, "A normal workday" in Define Events): after The
   Briefing she has started dressing differently for work, and the staff notices. I can tell her it suits her, or
   tell her to button up, which she does without a question. A line changes after A Knock at Night.
   After The Crawl (intimacy tier 3, MICRO_EVENTS_PLAN.md) I can tell her to undo one more instead, for the rest of
   the day; it needs some Exhibition, and $brian.name walks into a door. */
<<MicroContext $mom>>
<div class="activity-image-wrapper" style="max-height: 400px">
	<<DisplayActivity $mom>>
</div>
<p>$mom.callName's blouse today is one I haven't seen before: cream silk, soft enough that it moves a moment after she does, with one button less done up than she would have allowed herself a month ago. On anybody else, she'd have called it 'a bit much for the office'.</p>
<p>She's leaning over $darius.name's desk to point at something on his screen. $darius.name looks at the screen with tremendous discipline. Across the room, $ethan.name has stopped typing, and from the way $brian.name is staring at the inside of his own monitor, he's noticed $ethan.name noticing.</p>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
	{ who: $mom, text: "...so if we move the invoice to the fifteenth, they'll still pay on time, they just won't notice they're paying on time. Does that make sense, honey?" },
	{ who: $darius, text: "It makes perfect sense. It's a very elegant solution, actually. The invoice, I mean." },
	{ text: "She straightens up and catches me watching. Her hand goes to the open button at her collar, rests there for a second and doesn't do anything with it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<br>
<div id="mom-blouse-choice" class="choices">
	<div>
		<<link "Tell her it suits her">>
			<<replace "#mom-blouse-choice">>
				<p>I catch her later at the coffee machine, where nobody can hear us over the grinder.</p>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ who: $mom, text: "Is it too much? It's been hanging in the back of my closet for years with the tags still on, and this morning I just thought, well, why not, you know?" },
					{ who: $player, text: "It's not too much. It looks really good on you. You should wear it again." },
					{ who: $mom, text: "Oh. Okay, then." },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<<if setup.questDone("mom_nightVisit")>>
					<<silently>>
					<<set _msgs to [
						{ text: "She keeps stirring her coffee, around and around, though she hasn't put anything in it. Her voice drops." },
						{ who: $mom, text: "Is that for work, sweetie? Or is that for..." },
						{ text: "She doesn't finish the question, and I don't answer the half she asked. She picks up her mug and walks back to her desk, and she doesn't fix the button." },
					]>>
					<</silently>>
					<<Chat _msgs>>
				<<else>>
					<p>She says it to her coffee. Then she smooths the silk over her stomach with her free hand, as if she's only now feeling what she put on this morning.</p>
				<</if>>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "MomLust" 2>>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 1>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
	<div>
		<<link "Tell her to button up">>
			<<replace "#mom-blouse-choice">>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ text: "I wait until she passes my desk." },
					{ who: $player, text: "Do that button up, would you?" },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<p>She doesn't ask why. She glances around the room, quick, the way you'd check a street for traffic, to see who else got a look at her before I said anything. Then she does it right there, still walking, without slowing down, and her cheeks go pink while her fingers work the button closed.</p>
				<p>$ethan.name starts typing again a moment later.</p>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 1>>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "Efficiency" 1>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
	<<if _mc.tier >= 3>>
		<div>
			<<if _mc.exhibition < 10>>
				<span class="choice-locked">Tell her to undo one more<small>she isn't that bold yet</small></span>
			<<else>>
				<<link "Tell her to undo one more">>
					<<replace "#mom-blouse-choice">>
						<<silently>>
						<<set _msgs to [
							{ text: "I wait until she passes my desk on her way to the printer, and say it without looking up from my screen." },
							{ who: $player, text: "One more button. For the rest of the day." },
							{ text: "She stops beside my chair. For a moment she just stands there with the papers held against her chest. Then she moves them to one arm, and undoes the next button with the other hand, right there, and the next one too, for good measure, and smooths the silk flat again." },
							{ who: $mom, text: "Like this, honey?" },
							{ text: "The lace edge of her bra shows now when she breathes. I nod, and she goes on to the printer, and doesn't hurry." },
						]>>
						<</silently>>
						<<Chat _msgs>>
						<p>On her way back she has to pass $brian.name's desk. He's on his feet, carrying a box of parts toward the meeting room, and he looks up at the wrong moment and walks straight into the door frame with his shoulder, hard enough that something rattles in the box.</p>
						<<silently>>
						<<set _msgs to [
							{ who: $brian, text: "Sorry. Um. Door." },
							{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, sweetie, are you all right? Let me see." },
							{ text: "She puts her hand on his arm and bends a little to look at his shoulder, which brings the open blouse about a foot from his face. $brian.name stares at the ceiling tiles with tremendous concentration and says he's fine, he's fine, really, and goes into the meeting room and shuts the door." },
						]>>
						<</silently>>
						<<Chat _msgs>>
						<p>She comes back past my desk with a small, pleased look on her face that she smooths away before she sits down. She doesn't do the buttons up for the rest of the afternoon. $ethan.name gets very little done.</p>
						<<UpdateStat "+" "MomExhibition" 2>>
						<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 1>>
						<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 1>>
						<<Feel $mom "brian" 1>>
					<</replace>>
				<</link>>
			<</if>>
		</div>
	<</if>>
</div>
